Job description:1. Assist the HR manager to develop and optimize employee relationship management system;
2. Responsible for drafting, producing and signing labor contracts and other relevant agreements;
3. Handling employee recruitment, transfer, incentive and resignation;
4. Improve the company's personnel rules and regulations, answer employees' questions properly;
5. Handle employee complaints and internal labor disputes, and improve internal communication channels;
6. Cooperate with HR manager and legal counsel to handle labor disputes;
7. Plan employee activities to enrich company culture, enhance employee satisfaction and engagement, and establish harmonious relationship between employees and the company.

Job responsibilities: 
1. Responsible for game related model design and development; 
2. Responsible for game related tool design and development; 
3. Responsible for game optimization; 
 4. Responsible for automated script needed by games. 
 5. Drafting of related tech documents; 
 Job requirements: 
 1. More than 2 years of client development experience; 
 2. Proficiency in one of the these engines: Unity, Cocos, Laya. Has in-depth understanding of certain aspect of an engine, (i.e. UI, physics, animation, special effects, etc.). 
 3.  Able to optimize source codes and resources, understand certain game frameworks (IOC,MVC, ECS,MVVM, etc.), proficiency in object-oriented development and good coding practices.
